# Three-digit air temperature AND a three-digit feels-like - the widest the outdoor
# readout can ever be, and an ordinary Alexandria July afternoon rather than an edge case.
#
# This scenario exists because it was missing. Every other scenario is two-digit, so the
# 64x64's readout was first sized at 24px off "88 97" and rendered fine everywhere - while
# "101 114" needs 28px and ran its last digit and the degree dot off the right edge of the
# panel. Nothing would have shown that until a hot day in July, on a clock hanging on a
# wall, where it reads as a glitch rather than as a layout bug.
#
# Pair it with windchill.scn, which covers the other extreme: '-' advances a full 4px, so
# "-12 -20" is also 28px. Between the two, both ends of the width budget are pinned.
time         2026-07-21 15:20:00
temp         101
humidity     78
feels_like   114
sensor_dead  false
trains       6 13 21 29
bluetrains   4 11 18 26
event        Pool day
event_days   3
flight       AA123
flight_dest  MI
weather      fixtures/open-meteo-summer.json
